From: Caboose <caboose@local>
Subject: [PATCH 91/91] Free batched descriptor sets under the encoder lock and allocate unwritten ones

With batched descriptor sets, freeing a set the device already allocated sends
vkFreeDescriptorSets from the tracker, where no encoder lock is held, and the call was
encoded without taking it. It wrote the device stream while other threads were writing it:
their commands interleaved and the decoder read neither ("Failed to try unbox
VkDescriptorSet", the process lost), with or without guest-chosen set ids. It also skipped
what the lock sends first: WAIT_SERIAL for speculated waits (patch 0089).
A process that waited for a batch (answered at once) and then freed the batch's sets had the
phone free them before the batch ran; lavapipe then read a freed set in
handle_descriptor_sets and the Linux executor faulted. The free now takes the lock like any
command.

A submit whose bound sets had nothing written since the last commit sent no commit at all,
also when one of them was newly allocated: a set bound with no descriptor written (one a
shader never reads, one of immutable samplers) was never allocated on the device, which
bound a set it did not have. The commit now goes out whenever an allocation is pending.
---
diff --git a/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan_enc/ResourceTracker.cpp b/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan_enc/ResourceTracker.cpp
--- a/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan_enc/ResourceTracker.cpp
+++ b/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan_enc/ResourceTracker.cpp
@@ -1030,8 +1030,12 @@
         }
     }
 
-    // Skip out if there's nothing to VkWriteDescriptorSet home about.
-    if (writesForHost.empty()) {
+    // Skip out if there's nothing to VkWriteDescriptorSet home about. Caboose: a set bound
+    // with nothing written since its allocation (a set a shader never reads, one of immutable
+    // samplers) is still allocated on the device here; skipping it left the device binding a
+    // set it never had.
+    if (writesForHost.empty() &&
+        std::find(pendingAllocations.begin(), pendingAllocations.end(), 1u) == pendingAllocations.end()) {
         return;
     }
 
@@ -1342,7 +1346,11 @@
             unregister_VkDescriptorSet(sets[i]);
             delete_goldfish_VkDescriptorSet(sets[i]);
         } else {
-            enc->vkFreeDescriptorSets(device, ds->reified->pool, 1, &sets[i], false /* no lock */);
+            // Caboose: no encoder lock is held here (vkFreeDescriptorSets reaches the tracker
+            // directly), so the free takes it like any command: other threads share the
+            // device stream, and the lock sends WAIT_SERIAL for speculated waits first, so
+            // the phone frees no set a batch the process waited for may still use.
+            enc->vkFreeDescriptorSets(device, ds->reified->pool, 1, &sets[i], true /* do lock */);
         }
     }
 }
